<BaseLayout title="About MathGraph — Evidence and provenance" description="MathGraph publishes source-pinned mathematical objects and bounded verification evidence. A research project developed by Metalogic Labs." currentPath="/about/">
  <header class="section section--compact"><div class="shell">
    <div class="eyebrow">About MathGraph</div>
    <h1>Evidence should remain inspectable without the platform that published it.</h1>
    <p class="lede">MathGraph is a research-stage project developed by Metalogic Labs. It publishes source-pinned mathematical objects, explicit verification boundaries, portable replay contracts, and unresolved results.</p>
  </div></header>
  <section class="section"><div class="shell grid"><div class="span-7 prose">
    <h2>What is available</h2>
    <p>The current public site contains a 13-module Mathlib source catalogue, two immutable bounded evidence records, offline consumers, advisory discovery output, and one qualified finite capability profile. Source-indexed references support navigation; they are not proof dependencies or independently checked theorems.</p>
    <h2>Verification remains with the verifier</h2>
    <p>Native checkers and their declared trust boundaries remain authoritative. A successful historical receipt does not automatically establish current applicability, broader correctness, or permission to act. General hosted verification and continuous requalification are not implemented.</p>
    <p>The repository's source is publicly available for inspection. A project-wide open-source license has not been confirmed; third-party material remains subject to its original terms.</p>
  </div><aside class="span-5 callout"><strong>Source attribution</strong><p>References to independent public projects identify the sources of tested artifacts. They do not imply partnership, sponsorship, or institutional endorsement.</p></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
